        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "02f60e4a-d043-51eb-9946-ab9bca1d1ba5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: WonderWorks, A Little Princess\n- Companies: The Walt Disney Company, PBS\n- People: Frances Hodgson Burnett, Stephen Manes, Manuel Arce, Carl Haber, Amanda Plummer\n- Topics: children's books, television anthology series, made-for-TV movies\n\nFacts:\n- In 1905, Frances Hodgson Burnett published A Little Princess as a children's novel.\n- From 1984 to 1992, WonderWorks ran as an anthology television series.\n- WonderWorks was co-produced by The Walt Disney Company and PBS.\n- WonderWorks adapted acclaimed children's books into short made-for-TV movies.\n- WonderWorks included A Little Princess among its titles.\n- WonderWorks also included Gryphon, A Girl of the Limberlost, Sweet 15, A Waltz Through the Hills, The Canterville Ghost, Frog, The Haunting of Barney Palmer, Caddie Woodlawn, The House of Dies Drear, and The Boy Who Loved Trolls.\n- The WonderWorks title Gryphon was produced by Manuel Arce and Carl Haber and starred Amanda Plummer.\n- Stephen Manes was associated with a WonderWorks title mentioned in the chunk.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "877a5abf-dfea-5f27-988a-00e1f99fecf3",
        "text": "Page: WonderWorks. Sentence: WonderWorks was an anthology series which ran from 1984 to 1992 co-produced by The Walt Disney Company and PBS that made short, made for TV movies out of acclaimed children's books.\nPage: WonderWorks. Sentence: (by Stephen Manes), \"Gryphon\" (produced by Manuel Arce and Carl Haber, starring Amanda Plummer), \"A Little Princess\", \"A Girl of the Limberlost\", \"Sweet 15\", \"A Waltz Through the Hills\", \"The Canterville Ghost\", \"Frog,\" \"The Haunting of Barney Palmer\", \"Caddie Woodlawn\", \"The House of Dies Drear\", and \"The Boy Who Loved Trolls\".\nPage: A Little Princess. Sentence: A Little Princess is a children's novel by Frances Hodgson Burnett, first published as a book in 1905.",
